"P3412474348" "First to the Mill"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DeskClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2442767935" "Heavily Censored Memo"
// DetailString :
"P4010164838" "This memo is from the Rhode Island Department of Corrections, but most of the key references are blacked out. It refers to construction of some sort of facility, but it's unclear where the facility was built or for what purpose."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CabinetClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P994715718" "Irate Letter"
// DetailString :
"P3245283019" "This letter appears to have been written a U.S. Senator from the 1940s. He appears concerned with a 'Project Marduk', and the secrecy surrounding it. He also refers to anonymous 'private partners', and requests their identities. Given that you found the letter amongst other discarded and ignored mail, you can only assume that his requests were denied."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SafeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1544336196" "Facility Blueprints"
// DetailString :
"P3291164366" "You found a series of blueprints for what looks like a prison, though large sections of it appear to be missing. The blueprints were accompanied by a cryptic letter referring to a company named Milestone Labs, SPC. The letter seemed to indicate that unknown tech was being integrated into the prison's construction."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PandorasBoxHeroArc3Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P978500819" "Zigursky Blueprints"
// tDetailString :
"P3632745159" "These blueprints are what finally led you to Pandora's Box. For a while, it seemed as though everyone wanted their hands on the power of the gods. Who knows what terrible deeds they would have wrought, but thankfully, you were...<br><br><color gold><b>First to the Mill</b></color><br><br>You went to check in on Harvan's progress with the Antikythera, hoping that soon it would lead you and the Freedom Phalanx to the location of Pandora's Box. While you were visiting Fort Trident, however, an alert sounded in the base - Talos Island was under heavy assault!<br><br>At Citadel's behest, you took a portal to Talos Island, where you confronted Odysseus and Captain Castillo. Why they were working together, and what they were even in Talos for, remained a mystery to you. After you defeated their forces, Citadel arranged for the attackers to be shipped off to the Zig.<br><br>Shortly thereafter, Doctor Harvan came to you with a personal request. He wanted you to investigate an abandoned government office on the outskirts of Paragon City. His interest was in the fate of his late father, but what you found was cryptic information about a prison built in the 1950s.<br><br>When you returned to Harvan with your findings, it quickly became clear that something was missing from the picture... and that something, you deduced, was likely the very artifact you were looking for.<br><br>You immediately arranged to enter Zigursky, with Fusionette and Doctor Harvan in tow. Immediately upon entering the inmate area, you sensed that something was wrong - the guards were all missing. At that moment, you were ambushed by Odysseus, Castillo, and their followers. Luckily for you, the Antikythera prevented Zigursky's power-drain from affecting you, and you easily dispatched the inmates.<br><br>Underneath Zigursky, you found what you were looking for: Pandora's Box. However, proximity to Pandora's Box set off a reaction in Fusionette, causing her to go berserk and attack you. Seeing your fight with Fusionette, Harvan determined that the Box itself was causing her instability, and made to open it.<br><br>Unfortunately, rather than granting its power to those nearby, Pandora's Box exploded, releasing creatures of pure energy. You managed to fight them off long enough to allow the three of you to escape, but there's no telling where the energy from Pandora's Box has gone now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - HarvanTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P104051171" "{HeroName}, good to see you again. What can I do for you?"
// Answer Text :
"P3318344442" "Flashfire told me that you might be able to use my help."
// Page Harvan1 Text :
"P4128623897" "Ah yes, quite. Positron has already offered to take readings for me at various points in Paragon City.<br><br>I've been taking the data he gathers and feeding it through the metrics I've already gleaned from the Antikythera. So far, we've covered about half of the city, but we'll need more data points before I can accurately-"
// Answer Text :
"P3996305408" "Hm?"
// Page ClosePage Text :
"P856364347" ""
// Page NotTaskOwner Text :
"P2620207394" "<color skyblue>Only the team leader can cause the mission to progress through dialogue."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - CitadelTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P1298095924" "<color orange>Citadel remains focused on the screen in front of him, even after calling you over.</color><br><br>{HeroName}, it appears that Talos Island is currently under siege. I believe that a response from us will be necessary, given the magnitude of the assault. Is this a task you would be well-suited for?"
// Answer Text :
"P477387921" "I've taken down plenty of Raiders in my day, if that's what you're asking."
// Answer Text :
"P514723302" "Why not send the whole Phalanx?"
// Page Phalanx Text :
"P3259352882" "While I am aware that increasing the size of the response team would improve success rate, I am not certain that this attack is entirely genuine. I estimate that there is a 28.73% chance that the assault in Talos is intended to divert our attention for some reason. With Positron already outside the base's perimeter, the staff on-hand at the Phalanx base is limited.<br><br>Positron has informed me that the protection of Doctor Harvan is of paramount importance. Thus, I believe it would be best if a small but capable force was sent to deal with this incident."
// Answer Text :
"P2809254809" "Still, I could use the backup."
// Page OpenPortal Text :
"P2407805845" "<color orange>Citadel nods, still staring at the screen. Images flicker by, faster than the eye can see.</color><br><br>Fusionette has been stationed here since your encounter with Lilitu; Positron and Doctor Harvan both expressed interest in further studying her current condition.<br><br>Given that they are both preoccupied at the moment, I believe it would be best if Fusionette accompanied you. By monitoring your battle remotely, I will be able to measure her energy output. The data may prove useful in future tests.<br><br><color orange>Citadel's screen lets out a series of upbeat <i>bleeps</i>, and you hear a soft humming sound behind you.</color><br><br>I have calibrated the nearby portal to take you directly to the area of Talos that is under attack. Good luck, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P2890855340" "Thanks, Citadel. I'm off."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - PenelopeTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P841137558" "<color orange>Penelope seems to be staring at Harvan, brow furrowed. She doesn't notice you as you approach, until you're nearly face-to-face. When she finally does take notice of her surroundings, Penelope jumps slightly in surprise.</color><br><br>Oh! {HeroName}. You caught me off-guard. What's up?"
// Answer Text :
"P542571246" "Something about Harvan interest you?"
// Page Penelope1 Text :
"P3865068373" "<color orange>Penelope's face scrunches into a puzzled expression.</color><br><br>I'm... not sure, {HeroName}. Something's up with that guy. He gives me a weird vibe."
// Answer Text :
"P187893258" "Care to elaborate?"
// Page Penelope2 Text :
"P4183867837" "It's not something I can put my finger on. He's not planning to betray us or anything. I'd sense it, if he was. There's just something wrong about him.<br><br>He just... I don't know, <i>smells</i> wrong. Except, he doesn't... it's hard to describe. Just be careful around him, {HeroName}. He's not malicious, but I'm not sure I fully trust him, either."
// Answer Text :
"P3521974461" "Duly noted, Penelope."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - FusionetteTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2314886636" "<color orange>Fusionette beams at you.</color><br><br>Yo, {HeroName}! How's it going? Still kicking butt and taking names?"
// Answer Text :
"P3535977707" "Yeah, sure. How have you been feeling, lately?"
// Page Fusionette1 Text :
"P1354892841" "<color orange>Fusionette seems puzzled by the question at first.</color><br><br>What, you mean this?<br><br><color orange>She makes a broad gesture, looking herself over.</color><br><br>Never had a day when I felt better in my <b>life</b>, {HeroName}. It's fantastic. It's like that moment when you bring down an AV, or when you learn a new power, only <i>all the time</i>. Completely and utterly exhilarating."
// Answer Text :
"P1114873817" "No noticable side effects?"
// Page Fusionette2 Text :
"P978420087" "You mean, other than being my own light source? Naw, not that I've noticed.<br><br><color orange>Fusionette pauses for a moment, frowning.</color><br><br>Well, Jimmy did comment that I was getting a bit... <i>testy</i> recently. Although, really, I think he's just a little put off. I'm way stronger than he is, now, and he just can't seem to handle it.<br><br>Serously, though, that's the way things are, right? The strong survive, and keep getting stronger, while the weak fall away..."
// Answer Text :
"P939069396" "Fusionette... do you really believe that?"
// Page Fusionette3 Text :
"P2788535835" "<color orange>Fusionette winces, as though in pain, and puts a hand to her temple.</color><br><br>Um... I don't know, {HeroName}. I guess... I guess you're right, that seems a little off. Maybe I owe Jimmy an apology.<br><br><color orange>Fusionette rolls her head around, cracking her neck. She looks off at nothing, scowling slightly.</color><br><br>It's hard to think straight in here, {HeroName}. I'm way too cooped up. Positron wanted me to hang around so he can study me, but I need to cut loose.<br><br>Just promise me you'll take me along if you go do something interesting, ok? I don't think I can stand another moment in here."
// Answer Text :
"P2555586724" "Yeah... sure. I'll try to keep you included."

